From 48a42891731529eac11e343445bcf04cf6b0e2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:16:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] http, apt: Log eShop SOAP results and error applet codes

The eShop, ECS/IAS/CAS and NUS answer HTTP 200 and report failures
inside the SOAP body, so a title could stop with an error screen while
the log only showed successful requests.

- http:C logs the operation, ErrorCode and ErrorMessage (or SOAP
  faultstring) of every XML SOAP reply: info for success, warning for
  errors. Nothing else from the body is logged.
- apt StartLibraryApplet logs the error code ("005-5928") or error text
  an application passes to the error applet, also when the applet runs
  as LLE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
